+In each color-pair relation, the equation a*x+b*y+g=e identifies one excluded
+perfect matching. Those marked pairs form a graph on n*p vertices. The planted
+vertices are an isolated n-clique/component, so ordinary connected components
+find them in O(n^2*p) time. The reference implementation measures that scan.
+The no-tool route composes the marked affine maps around colors 0,1,2 to solve
+one fixed point, then propagates it along the color-0 row. At hard this costs
+241 field operations, versus roughly 715,000 mechanical visits.
