@@ -0,0 +1,222 @@
+# arXiv 2009.14171 — stable HR-LQ matching generator
+
+> Status: the module and local gates are complete, but the required external
+> hardening evidence is **pending**. On 2026-09-05 `harden.py` received HTTP 403
+> “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” from OpenRouter on every redraw. The
+> script-owned error transcript is preserved; it is not a hardness claim.
+
+| Profile | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B** — an efficient algorithm is disclosed |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite field |
+| Computational core | CSP/SAT |
+| Certificate | integer tuple: one open vertex hospital per color |
+| Intended intuition | invariant — marked affine relations share one consistency component |
+| Domain essentiality | licensed reduction |
+| Reduction | paper-central, Section 3.2, Theorem 2 |
+
+## Problem and trust model
+
+[Boehmer and Heeger, *A Fine-Grained View on Stable Many-To-One Matching
+Problems with Lower and Upper Quotas*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.14171)
+defines HR-LQ stability using feasible open hospitals, blocking pairs, and
+blocking coalitions. Theorem 2 reduces regular Multicolored Independent Set to
+an HR-LQ instance with five residents per color. This generator hands the
+solver those residents, quota-3 vertex hospitals, quota-4 edge hospitals, the
+penalizing gadgets, and exact strict preferences. The regular graph is stated
+succinctly by prime-field predicates rather than listing millions of edge
+hospitals. An answer selects one vertex hospital per color and thereby denotes
+the theorem's complete matching. `verify` checks, with exact modular arithmetic,
+that no selected pair opens a blocking quota-4 edge hospital; it never reads
+`inst["answer"]` and accepts every valid transversal.
+
+Generation is inverse, not search: labels `x_c` are sampled first and each
+relation is assembled so `a*x_c+b*x_d+g=e`. Because `e` is a quadratic residue
+explicitly excluded from the ordinary residue edges, the selected vertices are
+nonadjacent. Theorem 2 then produces the stable matching certificate.
+
+## Why this is Track B
+
+Track A would be false. The uniquely excluded pairs form a graph on `n*p`
+color-label vertices. The planted vertices are an isolated `n`-vertex
+component, so connected components recover a certificate in `O(n²p)` time. At
+the hard preset the measured reference pass examines 178,770 undirected marked
+edges and averages 721,140 insertion/scan/vertex operations (roughly 0.10--0.22 s in
+repeated local self-tests; the exact recorded value is in the JSON report).
+The compact route composes the marked affine maps around colors 0, 1, and 2 to
+find one fixed point, then propagates it through the color-0 row: 241 exact
+field operations. That gap—not average-case intractability—is the claimed
+no-tool difficulty.
+
+The parameter restrictions matter. Theorem 4 makes HR-LQ polynomial-time in
+`O(N³m)` when every lower quota is at most two, so this family retains the
+quota-3/4 hospitals of Theorem 2. Observation 3 gives `O(Nm)` time when the open
+hospital set is supplied, and Corollary 1 gives `O(Nm·2^m_quota)`; both confirm
+that choosing the open vertex hospitals is the load-bearing part. The number of
+colors grows rather than remaining a small FPT parameter.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=0`)
+
+Here `n=3`, `p=7`, and the relation table is:
+
+```text
+c d a b g e
+0 1 4 1 3 2
+0 2 5 4 4 2
+1 2 3 4 4 2
+```
+
+The full rendered conventions are: color `c` has vertices `v(c,0)` through
+`v(c,6)`; `v(c,x)` and `v(d,y)` are adjacent exactly when
+`z=(a*x+b*y+g) mod 7` is a nonzero quadratic residue other than `e`. There is a
+quota-3 hospital `V(c,x)` for every vertex and a quota-4 hospital for every
+edge. Residents `A(c)` and `B(c)` rank vertex blocks in forward and reverse
+label order, putting the incident edge hospitals immediately before their
+vertex hospital. `S(c)` ranks all vertex hospitals, then `P(c,1)>P(c,2)`;
+`T(c): P(c,2)>P(c,3)` and `U(c): P(c,3)>P(c,1)`, with each `P` hospital having
+quota 2. The output pairs denote assignments of `A,B,S` to the selected `V`
+and `T,U` to `P(c,3)`.
+
+```python
+answer = [[0, 6], [1, 3], [2, 6]]
+verify(inst, answer)  # (True, "ok")
+verify(inst, [[0, 3], [1, 3], [2, 6]])
+# (False, "blocking edge-hospital coalition at colors 0,1 with labels 3,3")
+```
+
+A person can solve this demo by hand: set each of the three affine forms equal
+to its excluded value `e` and solve the three linear congruences modulo 7. The
+demo has 125 valid certificates in the broader nonadjacency language, so the
+displayed one is not privileged by the checker.
+
+<details><summary>Complete rendered demo statement</summary>
+
+```text
+Find a stable matching in the following Hospital Residents instance with lower
+quotas (HR-LQ). Work in GF(7), represented by 0,...,6. There are three colors,
+and color c has vertices v(c,x), x=0,...,6. For a row c d a b g e, vertices
+v(c,x) and v(d,y) are adjacent exactly when z=(a*x+b*y+g) mod 7 is a nonzero
+quadratic residue and z != e.
+
+c d a b g e
+0 1 4 1 3 2
+0 2 5 4 4 2
+1 2 3 4 4 2
+
+Every vertex has (3-1)*(7-3)/2 incident edges and there are no same-color
+edges. A hospital is closed or open with at least its lower quota; every upper
+quota is 16. An open acceptable hospital blocks if a resident prefers it to
+their assignment. A closed h has a blocking coalition if l(h) acceptable
+residents all prefer h. Stability means feasibility and no block.
+
+For each c,x there is V(c,x), quota 3. For each graph edge there is
+E(c,x,d,y), c<d, quota 4. For each c there are P(c,1),P(c,2),P(c,3), quota 2.
+Residents A(c),B(c),S(c),T(c),U(c) have these strict preferences:
+
+* A(c): process x=0,...,6; within each block put all incident E hospitals in
+  lexicographic order, followed by V(c,x).
+* B(c): the same blocks in order x=6,...,0.
+* S(c): V(c,0)>...>V(c,6)>P(c,1)>P(c,2).
+* T(c): P(c,2)>P(c,3).
+* U(c): P(c,3)>P(c,1).
+
+Only those residents accept the listed hospitals: V(c,x) is accepted by A,B,S;
+an edge hospital by A,B at each endpoint; and P(c,1),P(c,2),P(c,3) by
+{S,U},{S,T},{T,U}. Hospital rankings are immaterial because exactly l(h)
+residents accept h.
+
+Return one [c,x_c] per color in color order. It denotes the matching assigning
+A(c),B(c),S(c) to V(c,x_c), and T(c),U(c) to P(c,3); all other hospitals close.
+Different colors may repeat a numeric label.
+
+Give the final answer inside <answer></answer> as exactly three JSON pairs
+[[0,x_0],[1,x_1],[2,x_2]], with each label in 0,...,6. Syntax example:
+<answer>[[0,0],[1,1],[2,2]]</answer>. Put nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+</details>
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | Colors `n` | Prime/classes `p` | Residents | Edge hospitals (implicit) | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 3 | 7 | 15 | 42 | hand example; not hardened |
+| easy | 16 | 29 | 80 | 45,240 | oracle run could not start |
+| medium | 32 | 59 | 160 | 819,392 | not reached |
+| hard | 60 | 101 | 300 | 8,759,730 | intended shipping preset, pending oracle |
+
+`escalate` increases `p` while holding `n` and the answer length fixed.
+
+## Gate measurements
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted and compact-route checks |
+| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged fenced JSON round-trips; garbage returns `None` |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware random candidates |
+| G5 | pass locally | shipping density 0/200,000; demo exact count 125; reference 8/8 |
+| G6 | pass locally | four attacks each 0/8; disclosed reference algorithm 8/8 |
+| G7 | pass | doubled `n=120` builds/verifies; answer has 240 atoms |
+| G8 | pass | 80/80 invariance and real-map checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 471 chars, about 118 tokens, 120 atoms; 241 route operations |
+| G9(a,b) | pending | no successful OpenRouter call; no verdict asserted |
+
+## Oracle and G9 evidence
+
+| Arm/run | Preset | Successful attempts | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare hardening | easy | 0 | four HTTP 403 key-limit errors; script aborted |
+| hinted | — | 0/0 | not run |
+| placebo | — | 0/0 | not run |
+
+There is therefore no hinted-minus-placebo conclusion yet. When API capacity is
+restored, rerun the bare loop first, then run the hinted and placebo copies in
+separate directories as required by the task. Do not treat the current error
+rows as oracle failures.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import gen_2009_14171 as g
+
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=123, **g.DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+statement = g.render(inst)
+answer = inst["answer"]                 # held only by the dataset builder
+assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
+assert g.parse_answer(
+    "result: <answer>" + __import__("json").dumps(answer) + "</answer>"
+) == answer
+```
+
+After valid hardening evidence exists, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 2009.14171 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- This is a paper-licensed reduction, not unreduced native-domain coverage. The
+  solver's real search core is a multicolored binary CSP, although the full
+  HR-LQ matching and preference semantics remain visible and are verified.
+- The prime-field predicate is a succinct representation of a very large
+  ordinary graph. The paper proves Theorem 2 for explicit regular graphs; the
+  succinct formula defines the same finite objects but adds exploitable affine
+  structure not analyzed by the paper.
+- The family becomes easy with code: connected components of the marked
+  exclusions are decisive. That success is the Track-B baseline, not an attack
+  failure concealed as hardness.
+- The 0/200,000 density estimate is under the exact prior a statement-aware
+  solver gets for free—one field label per color. It does not estimate a solver
+  biased toward the marked affine relations.
+- Tested attacks are equal-degree/min-label, forward greedy, 256 uniform
+  restarts, and a zero-anchor marked ansatz. No industrial SAT/CP solver or SDP
+  relaxation was run; the exact connected-components decoder is stronger for
+  this generated promise, but may not model every heuristic.
+- `canonical_key` uses all marked triangle and four-cycle types and is invariant
+  under the tested arbitrary relabelings. It is not a complete colored-graph
+  isomorphism algorithm, so rare non-isomorphic collisions remain possible.
+- The mandatory four-vendor bare and G9 runs remain the blocking item. The
+  current `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` contains only script-authored API errors.
