codex
Outcome: rejected—no generator is being shipped.

Theorem 2 supports inverse generation and exact verification, so G and V pass. H fails:

- Track A: every generated instance has a deterministic affine decoder.
- Track B: the mechanical and compact routes coincide at 241 field operations plus scanning 1,770 rows.
- The decisive in-context attack succeeded 8/8 locally.
- Official oracles solved 7/8 scored instances, including both completed hard attempts.

OpenRouter exhausted its quota before the third hard attempt; errors were not counted as failures.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2009.14171/REJECTED.md)
- [Retained prototype](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2009.14171/rejected_gen_2009_14171.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2009.14171/selftest_report.json)
- [Oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2009.14171/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2009.14171/README.md)

The rejection cites the paper’s definitions, Theorems 1, 2, and 4, Observation 3, and Corollary 1. I did not run `submit.sh --reject` because it commits and pushes repository state.
